    "narrative": "For the May 13th slate, the Zurich Zebras\u2019 lineup is anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (81.46) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.59), who represent our highest-upside plays. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in core piece, boasting an elite 0.423 xwOBA, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** presents the day's premier opportunistic value; he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Ritchie and his 5.68 xERA. Given that Stolen Bases are the scarcest commodity in our build, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is prioritized heavily here, as his dynamic platoon edge and speed potential significantly outweigh his lower spot in the order. **Luke Raley** also warrants attention (62.83) due to a soft matchup against McCullers Jr., where his capacity to exploit a slow delivery profile\u2014boosting his stolen base probability\u2014adds a strategic layer to his power-heavy projection.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the exclusion of **Trea Turner**, who remains on the bench due to status uncertainty. Despite a strong base profile, his lack of confirmation in the official lineup rendered him a zero in today\u2019s efficiency model, effectively yielding his spot to **Caleb Durbin** (53.47). While **Caleb Durbin** sits in the nine-hole, his aggressive base-running upside in a park that favors his profile makes him a safer aggregate play than risking a zero from an unconfirmed **Trea Turner**. We are also closely monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (40.89); his score is suppressed by a difficult platoon split against Scott and a modest order position, forcing him toward the floor of our starting threshold. While the Zebras have a solid offensive baseline today, we must remain cautious of the volatility inherent in our middle-infield selections and the potential for late-game defensive substitutions to impact our cap usage.",
